{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSix ADRs carry stale or unmarked status: 0010 (amended by 0021, `0021…md:3`), 0013 (amended by 0020, `0020…md:3,47-48`), 0029 (\"before the redesign\", `0029…md:5`), 0057 (`REBAR_LLM_MODEL` removed in v0.12.0: `CHANGELOG.md:569`, under the `## [0.12.0] - 2026-08-15` heading at `:543`, tombstone `src/rebar/_deprecations.py:248`, commit `abf3817187bf`, ticket `6cc4-56f1-6cc6-4c7f`), 0083 (`:5-6` \"Phase 2 in progress under epic bbf1\" — `bbf1-82e1-cf9d-494a` doctorial-semiironic-wrasse is closed), 0092 (its \"Keep explicit compatibility adapters\" paragraph `:24-27` describes removed surfaces: ticket `82bb-439b-1c42-4abd` seagreen-wet-bluefish, commits `9e65567b79ff` + `e8fbf305057b`; `docs/release-notes.md:833` (\"BREAKING (pre-1.0) — legacy reconcile compatibility surfaces are removed\") and `CHANGELOG.md:213`; ADR 0111 `:33-35,85-88` cites 0092 as its carve-out).\n\n## Approach\n- **0010** (insert after `:3`, before `:5`): `> **Amended by [ADR 0021](0021-replication-change-refs.md) (2026-07-01).** The replicated data-ref set widened to include ` `refs/changes/*` `; the NON-force, mirror-off, deploy-key-identity decisions below stand unchanged.`\n- **0013** (insert after `:1`): `> **Amended by [ADR 0020](0020-two-vote-ci-gate.md) (2026-07-01).** Decision (1)'s single-vote / no-CI-` `Verified` ` statements are superseded by the two-vote gate; the ` `LLM-Review` ` label, its submit requirement and the ` `MaxNoBlock` ` caveat below stand.`\n- **0029** (insert after `:1`): `> **Context landed (2026-09-07).** The redesign this record precedes — epic ` `3006-e198-13db-4e1f` ` (file-lens-jewel) and child ` `444d-c21f-2c82-4622` ` (port-jar-withe, archived→Done) — is closed, and the archived-not-status-looped guardrail of Decision 2 is live (` `inbound_differ.py` `, \"ADR 0029 #2\"). Decisions 1–4 remain in force: [ADR 0103](0103-reconciler-operation-coordination.md) and [ADR 0107](0107-reconciler-typed-mutation-payload-contract.md) consume this arbitration unchanged. Not superseded.`\n- **0057** (insert after `:1`): `> **Amended (2026-08-12).** The deprecated ` `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` ` variable was REMOVED in v0.12.0 and is a tombstone (` `rebar._deprecations` `, tier ` `error` `: setting it fails loud) — ticket ` `6cc4-56f1-6cc6-4c7f` `. Read \"deprecated\" below as \"removed\"; the model-class slots are the only live interface.`\n- **0083** replace `:5-6` with: `- **Status:** Accepted (Phase 1 and Phase 2 landed — Phase 2 epic ` `bbf1-82e1-cf9d-494a` `, doctorial-semiironic-wrasse, closed; the backend interface pinned in §(d) is the live seam)`. Keep `:7-13`.\n- **0092** (a) insert after `:1`: `> **Amended (2026-09-04) — see §Amendment.** The compatibility adapters this ADR kept were removed by ticket ` `82bb-439b-1c42-4abd` `; only the engine-only ` `--filter-local-ids` ` post-filter survives.` (b) append after `:56`:\n  `## Amendment (2026-09-04) — the compatibility adapters were removed; only ` `--filter-local-ids` ` survives`\n  `Ticket ` `82bb-439b-1c42-4abd` ` (seagreen-wet-bluefish) removed, as a pre-1.0 BREAKING change, the top-level CLI ` `rebar reconcile` ` route, direct-engine ` `--mode reconcile-check` `, the Python ` `rebar.reconcile` ` facade, the MCP ` `reconcile` ` tool and the persisted ` `reconcile_diagnostics` ` status field (` `docs/release-notes.md` ` §\"legacy reconcile compatibility surfaces are removed\"). The Decision's \"Keep explicit compatibility adapters\" paragraph no longer describes the tree: ` `rebar bridge preview|sync|fsck|status` ` and their library/MCP twins are the only vocabulary. One adapter survives — the direct-engine legacy route's ` `--filter-local-ids` ` engine-only post-filter, restored by commit ` `e8fbf305057b` ` for live-DC harness scoping that ` `--only` ` cannot express for not-yet-bound inbound Jira keys. [ADR 0111](0111-no-internal-only-compatibility-shims.md) cites this ADR as its public compatibility-contract carve-out; that carve-out now covers exactly that one flag. The Consequences bullet \"Removing compatibility requires a separate deprecation decision\" was satisfied by the pre-1.0 removal pass recorded on that ticket.`\n- Do NOT edit 0111 (`tests/scripts/test_internal_shim_policy_docs.py:56-70` pins its critique wording). Run `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py` (no index change expected — the index is title-derived, `gen_adr_index.py:190-198`).\n\n## Cites re-measured on origin/main `d74d53a5ffd` (ADR cites verified individually; the CHANGELOG and release-notes evidence cites were corrected after review round 1)\nEvery citation above was re-measured against the tree before review; all resolve. `0010` title `:1`, existing number-note blockquote `:3`, `**Status:**` `:5`. `0013` `**Status:**` `:3`. `0029` `**Status:**` `:3` (list-item form), \"before the redesign\" `:5`. `0057` `**Status:**` `:3`. `0083` existing renumber blockquote `:3`, Status `:5-6` with \"Phase 2 in progress under epic `bbf1-82e1-cf9d-494a`\" on `:5`. `0092` `**Status:**` `:3`, the \"Keep explicit compatibility adapters\" paragraph `:24-27`, file length 56 lines so the amendment appends at the end. `0021:3` and `0020:3` are the `**Status:**` lines that record the amendments to 0010 and 0013.\n\n## Scope\n`docs/adr/0010-gerrit-github-replication.md`, `0013-llm-review-label.md`, `0029-reconciler-bidirectional-status-and-echo.md`, `0057-model-classes-and-the-rebar-llm-model-deprecation.md`, `0083-reconciler-vendor-adapter-seam.md`, `0092-bridge-primary-vocabulary-compatibility-adapters.md`. Not: 0042, 0090 (done), 0071, 0086, 0044, 0049, 0111.\n\n## Testing\n`python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` (bijection + no dangling `](NNNN-slug.md)` links); `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check`; `python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check`; `pytest tests/scripts/test_internal_shim_policy_docs.py tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_removal.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py` (old spellings are allowed under `docs/adr/`, `:22`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] **Five** of the six files — 0010, 0013, 0029, 0057, 0092 — gain exactly one new `> **…**` blockquote between the title and the `**Status:**` line (verify with `sed -n '1,8p'`). 0010 already carries a `> **Number note (story 0743):**` blockquote at `:3`, so its new one is inserted after it, before `**Status:**` at `:5`. **0083 gains no blockquote** — its change is the `:5-6` Status rewrite, which AC3 checks; an AC demanding a new blockquote in all six could not pass on a correct implementation. 0092 additionally has exactly one `## Amendment (2026-09-04)` heading (`grep -c` = 1).\n- [x] `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py && python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` exit 0; `git diff --stat -- docs/adr/README.md docs/adr/.numbers` is empty.\n- [x] `grep -n \"Phase 2 in progress\" docs/adr/0083-reconciler-vendor-adapter-seam.md` is empty."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793486832653733001,"uuid":"745fb081-2f5d-490d-afcf-0dd081d6f08e"}